commit d7eceb7c
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 15:39:11 -0600
subject: security(cors): replace wildcard CORS on web/fetch with configurable allowlist

Replace Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * on the web fetch endpoint with a
settings-driven origin allowlist. When corsAllowedOrigins is empty (the
default), legacy wildcard behavior is preserved for backward compatibility.
When non-empty, only listed origins receive CORS headers; disallowed browser
origins get no CORS headers (browser blocks), and server-side clients
(curl, SDKs) are unaffected since they don't send Origin headers.

Changes:
- src/shared/utils/cors.js: new resolveCorsHeaders() utility
- src/app/api/v1/web/fetch/route.js: use utility for OPTIONS + POST
- src/lib/db/repos/settingsRepo.js: add corsAllowedOrigins default
- tests/unit/cors-allowlist.test.js: 6 tests covering all paths

Fixes: GAP-P1-13 (security scan)


